  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "For two independent random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{5}{2}$ and $\\text{Var}[Y]=\\frac{1}{3}.$ Find $\\text{Var}[X-Y].$",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are independent random variables, then \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X\\pm Y]=\\text{Var}[X]+\\text{Var}[Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X-Y]=\\frac{5}{2}+\\frac{1}{3}=\\frac{17}{6}.\n$$",
